 "name": "Historical Irrigation Canals",
 "description": "Faithful replication of the photo questionnaire in Zhong, Zhang, Xia, Hao & Tan (2024), \"Public Aesthetic and Recreational Preferences for Historical Irrigation Canals in Rural Areas: A Case Study in Li Canal-Gaoyou Irrigation District\", Buildings 14(7):1955, doi:10.3390/buildings14071955. After an overview of all 18 photographs of main, branch and tertiary canals, participants see each photo in random order and rate (1–5) whether the scene is beautiful, evokes a sense of history and heritage, and appears unique with distinct local characteristics, then tick which of six recreational activities (walking, jogging, biking, swimming, boating, fishing) would suit it, or none. Then gender, age, education, income, rural living experience and prior awareness of historical irrigation structures / WHIS, with the paper's categories. Original sample: 465 valid questionnaires (373 online, 92 local residents), 2024. Photographs are the authors' own from Figure 3 of the open-access paper (CC BY 4.0), used with credit; the template is taken down if the authors object. Differences from the original study: (1) photos are cut from the published figure (about 685 × 455 px) and the photo numbers in the top-right corners were digitally removed, leaving a soft patch where the number sat over trees in three photos; (2) the separate cost section (24 intervention scenarios with relative costs) is left out; (3) the income period is not stated in the paper and the RMB bands are kept as reported; (4) the paper's offline paper version and IP-based local check are not reproduced.",
